Congratulations on your desire to quit smoking! You may have many reasons to stop smoking, from improved health to increased money saved to increased energy levels. Here are some suggestions to make it easier:

- Start small: Set a specific “quitting date” and prepare in advance for it, either by planning activities to take your mind off of it or by telling friends and family you intend to stop; 
- Talk to your friends: Use your smoking peers as sources of support when dealing with triggers to quit and don't be too hard on yourself if you don't make it;
- Practice positive thinking: Repeat positive affirmations ("I can do this," or "Quitting will make my life better") when dealing with negative thoughts;
- Manage triggers: Prepare strategies when anticipating when or where you tend to smoke (e.g., taking a different route when driving to a favourite place) and don't feel hard if they lead to relapse.

